sys: one tree, one pronoun, and messages
  One tree holds all you work on, from the root down to a note's parts,
  and cur, its one pronoun, names the thing you mean. You act on words:
  any text is an address, and a verb, as acme's buttons are, takes its
  noun from cur. A program follows cur and says what it shows, parts
  each of a kind, and never how; a view draws each kind its best, and
  one it does not know as its text. Nothing passes but messages, plain
  data in a file or a line, so any piece can be another process.
you             at a host: tmux, or gio's window
  act           keys, and the word a click is on
    → verbs     a word
  see           the frame, as each view draws it
surface         verbs on words, views of kinds
  verbs         c, p and p -a: this, look, do
    → cur       this
  views         the terminal, gio, the page
    → see       drawn
meaning         the thing meant, and what is shown
  cur           this, one a window
    → programs  followed
  kinds         what a program shows, never how
    → views     draw
work            on one tree
  programs      fm moves, ed types, the lens sees
    → cur       its row
    → kinds     what
    → tree      typed
  tree          files, down to a note's parts
    → programs  read, by its kind
